# Owner: control typed configuration -> releases.Load; string absolute protected JSON file.
# Optional feature: omit this key and YAML release_view_config_file to leave unavailable.
# Explicit empty/false/relative/unknown keys are rejected. No ambient environment lookup.
# File fields: directory (absolute readonly projection directory); scope_id (32 lowercase hex);
# manifest_sha256 and configuration_sha256 (64 lowercase hex, exact original scope bindings);
# publisher_uid (integer0..2147483647, actual owner, MUST differ from serving UID);
# page_size (integer1..100 records); operation_seconds (integer1..30 seconds, <= HTTP budget).
# All seven fields are required, with no implicit defaults. The example is nonworking.
# No credentials or raw scope root are accepted. JSON file follows original private0600 rules.
# Explicit --env-file overrides YAML reference; JSON is read by one typed owner at startup.
# Restart control after changing the reference/bindings/policy; snapshots reload on every GET.
PROJECT_ONE_RELEASE_VIEW_CONFIG_FILE=/run/projectone/config/admin-view.json
